                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1b88bbfa-7d11-3ca6-aaaf-b4e7cb54441a",
                        "entry_id": "48b4862f-10b6-3dcc-b50d-18fd770df157",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ekspresywne i wyraziste wyrecytowanie utworu literackiego"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "92f4f651-37c6-4f60-b3af-300e492f0290",
                                "sense_id": "1b88bbfa-7d11-3ca6-aaaf-b4e7cb54441a",
                                "text": "Po deklamacji Anity chór zaśpiewa pieśń legionową: „Wojenko, wojenko”."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "711a68bc-f88a-3d4d-9d1d-3bf869771446",
                        "entry_id": "48b4862f-10b6-3dcc-b50d-18fd770df157",
                        "glosses": [
                            "patetyczna i przesadzona wypowiedź, puste słowa"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c76dd44d-4c44-4b23-a882-0e30175a0ad3",
                                "sense_id": "711a68bc-f88a-3d4d-9d1d-3bf869771446",
                                "text": "Jego deklamacjami się nie przejmuj, jest przecież mistrzem frazesu."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d5cd0612-61fc-4b05-a37b-a624875f42ee",
                        "source_entry_id": "48b4862f-10b6-3dcc-b50d-18fd770df157",
                        "source_sense_id": "1b88bbfa-7d11-3ca6-aaaf-b4e7cb54441a",
                        "target_lang_word": "declamation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "declamation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cca41829-ea0c-35d6-9493-b6b53d0d7d29",
                                        "entry_id": "ab45a6fb-cc57-37da-983f-47f3d5d0f578",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act or art of declaiming; rhetorical delivery; loud speaking in public."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4cbf1447-10b3-37b0-b258-e93233afa82e",
                                        "entry_id": "ab45a6fb-cc57-37da-983f-47f3d5d0f578",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act or art of declaiming; rhetorical delivery; loud speaking in public.",
                                            "The public recitation of speeches as an exercise in schools and colleges."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3385cf05-1fb1-46bf-a663-ce4b444ccc54",
                                                "sense_id": "4cbf1447-10b3-37b0-b258-e93233afa82e",
                                                "text": "His recitations were prompt and correct, and his answers were given with confidence. But perhaps he did himself most credit in declamation. He had always been very fond of that, and though he had never received and scientific instruction in it, he possessed a natural grace and a deep feeling of earnestness which made success easy. He had selected an extract from Webster--the reply to the Hayne--and this was the showpiece of the afternoon. The rest of the declamation was crude enough, but Harry's impressed even the most ignorant of his listeners as superior for a boy of his age."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2cd73f13-b086-3d93-a0c1-80fbb7a4f8a0",
                                        "entry_id": "ab45a6fb-cc57-37da-983f-47f3d5d0f578",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A set or harangue; declamatory discourse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c02f8977-2051-3b0e-9b0c-92d733630287",
                                        "entry_id": "ab45a6fb-cc57-37da-983f-47f3d5d0f578",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pretentious rhetorical display, with more sound than sense."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "caf3f2d6-fee1-4900-8399-b9410b4b06b5",
                                                "sense_id": "c02f8977-2051-3b0e-9b0c-92d733630287",
                                                "text": "mere declamation"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eb7f761a-a38a-487b-961e-a3aa0b61e0e1",
                        "source_entry_id": "48b4862f-10b6-3dcc-b50d-18fd770df157",
                        "source_sense_id": "1b88bbfa-7d11-3ca6-aaaf-b4e7cb54441a",
                        "target_lang_word": "recitation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "recitation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bec46379-3395-3de6-8111-6a23b33e95cf",
                                        "entry_id": "f180acf2-2815-33a4-ba33-4ce399d9bc1a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of publicly reciting something previously memorized."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67995f52-4162-4b83-a25c-5a3ff2a0ba51",
                                                "sense_id": "bec46379-3395-3de6-8111-6a23b33e95cf",
                                                "text": "The recitation will air nationally and be featured at Raymond James Stadium in Tampa, Florida."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d40a80bc-8173-33e8-8a8e-36300fd3e499",
                                        "entry_id": "f180acf2-2815-33a4-ba33-4ce399d9bc1a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The material recited."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1052be93-a836-3c5e-80c0-8748a4a84c9b",
                                        "entry_id": "f180acf2-2815-33a4-ba33-4ce399d9bc1a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A regularly scheduled class, in a school, in which discussion occurs of the material covered in a parallel lecture."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86aebb4b-41a9-469e-917a-1cfdced437c4",
                                                "sense_id": "1052be93-a836-3c5e-80c0-8748a4a84c9b",
                                                "text": "I shall now endeavor to give some account of the College.... Some then go to a recitation of the lesson they have learnt the previous evening. Some return to their rooms till the breakfast-bell, about seven or after. At eight the sludy bell rings. All must then go in their rooms and continue there, even if they have no lessons to learn, unless they attend a recitation which occupies an hour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96b42321-200d-48cc-98ab-ec29dfd538e0",
                                                "sense_id": "1052be93-a836-3c5e-80c0-8748a4a84c9b",
                                                "text": "1896, Frank Norris, \"The 'English Courses' of the University of California\", reprinted in, 1986, Novels and Essays, Library of America, →ISBN, page 1109,\nIn the \"announcement of courses\" published annually by the faculty of the University of California the reader cannot fail to be impressed with the number and scope of the hours devoted by the students to recitations and lectures upon the subject of \"literature.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37c142ae-d3a3-4408-99b4-f1b50e310625",
                                                "sense_id": "1052be93-a836-3c5e-80c0-8748a4a84c9b",
                                                "text": "Many of my courses, however, were offered in recitation-lecture format. We would attend class, say twice a week, and a lecture once a week. ... I do seem to recall that my recitation sections seldom had less than 40 to 50 students and my lecture classes often had upwards of 100 to 300 students."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22cde048-06f0-3d97-a014-b9e59c534d2f",
                                        "entry_id": "f180acf2-2815-33a4-ba33-4ce399d9bc1a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A reiteration; a setting down, e.g. for ease of reference, of something previously established."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "49a7fec8-1350-3871-a6dc-e256b77a6373",
                                        "entry_id": "f180acf2-2815-33a4-ba33-4ce399d9bc1a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A part of a song's lyrics that is spoken rather than sung."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
